### **Cómo Obtener RoleDefinitionId**

```powershell
# Método 1: Extraer con el script
.\PIM-SecureAssignment-ARM.ps1 -ExtractRoles -ExportRolesCsv

# Método 2: Comando directo
Get-MgDirectoryRoleTemplate | Where-Object { $_.DisplayName -like "*Administrator*" } |
    Select-Object DisplayName, Id | Format-Table

# Método 3: Buscar rol específico
$role = Get-MgDirectoryRoleTemplate | Where-Object { $_.DisplayName -eq "Global Administrator" }
Write-Host "RoleDefinitionId: $($role.Id)"
```

